        "created_at": "2012-09-20T15:07:18.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I'm currently in the thought process of getting the proper attire for Cursed Acolyte (for those who don't have Infernal Relics yet, the Cursed Acolyte is a cultist in GloomWeaver's deck)&nbsp;so that way I could cosplay as myself. First thing I would need to do is figure out what his pants and footwear are. Secondly I would have to do a lot of push-ups to fit the right body type.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Cosplaying yourself? I've seen it before (Potential Sidekick), but that still bends my mind. Not to mention makes me laugh. The idea is just funny.</p>",
